# XSH raise()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.raise.001
anchor     functions/raise.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       raise(SIGUSR1) with a handler returns 0, after the handler has run
           and returned.
note       If the handler runs, raise() waits for it; whether it must
           run before raise() returns is standard question Q-11.
test       t/001-handler-before-return.c

assertion  XSH.raise.002
anchor     functions/raise.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       raise() in a thread sends the signal to that thread: the handler
           runs in the calling thread, and when the caller has the signal
           blocked it stays pending for that thread, not delivered to
           another thread that has it unblocked.
test       t/002-calling-thread.c

assertion  XSH.raise.003
anchor     functions/raise.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2001
says       raise() with signal number 100000 returns a non-zero value and sets
           errno to EINVAL.
test       t/003-einval.c
